// `#[attr]` above a positional call argument is a parse error, though the
// same attribute is accepted on a labeled argument's value and on an
// array element. Expected: parses (and `--check` passes). Actual: "Parse
// error at line 7 column 2 ... Unexpected `(` ... note: a `;` separates
// this statement from the one before".
let f = |x| x + 1;
f(#[native] 1 + 2)
